// UnitTests.src - the unit-test program for this workspace.
//
// Copied here from the DFUnit package by SetupUnitTests.bat. It has to live in your
// OWN AppSrc: DataFlex resolves a project name against the workspace's own AppSrc
// path only, never against a library's, so a copy inside the package could not be
// added as a project at all.
//
// Add it to the workspace's project list - in the Studio: right-click the workspace
// in the Solution Explorer > Add > Add Project - and compile it like any other
// program.
//
// Running it:
//     UnitTests64.exe                  the test-runner window
//     UnitTests64.exe -c               unattended: results on the console, then
//                                      exit 0 (all passed) or -1 (a test failed)
//     UnitTests64.exe -c -o result.xml the same, plus JUnit XML for a build server
//     UnitTests64.exe -n               open the window but do not run on startup
//
// Nothing else in this file needs to change - new tests are added by editing
// oUnit_Tests.pkg.

Use DFUnit.pkg

Object oApplication is a cApplication
    Set psCompany to "Your company"
    Set psProduct to "Unit Tests"
End_Object

Object oTestApplication is a cDFUnitTestApplication

    // Every test fixture in this workspace hangs off this one file.
    Use oUnit_Tests.pkg

End_Object

// Parses the command line, then either shows the test-runner window or runs the
// tests on the console and exits with the appropriate code.
Send AutoRun of ghoTestApplication
